                <pb facs="0983" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.01/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-11T23:00:00-04:00">March 11, 1936—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 12—12:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. From Braden. Department’s 30, March 11, 6 p.m. Argentine Minister Asunción
                    has informed Saavedra Lamas that Stefanich agrees to procedure outlined in my
                    57, March 10, 11 p.m. Therefore, he should have no objection to procedure of
                    identic notes.</p>
                <p>Will confer with Saavedra Lamas and other delegates tomorrow noon. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
